p.src:
The lecture gives us a clear sequence: $\begin{aligned}
\text{Need observed}
&\Rightarrow \text{interview decision-makers},\\
\text{Interview evidence}
&\Rightarrow \text{clearer statement of pain},\\
\text{Pain with business value}
&\Rightarrow \text{pilot commitment},\\
\text{Pilot commitment}
&\Rightarrow \text{build the }\mathrm{MVP}.\end{aligned}$ And it is important that the sequence not be inverted. We do not begin by pressing for a sale. We begin by asking what the client’s challenges are and what solving them would mean for the company. Only after that discussion has clarified the value do we ask for something stronger, namely a willingness to pilot the solution.

